2. Notice of modification (GPLv3 section 5(a))
----------------------------------------------

THIS IS A SUBSTANTIALLY MODIFIED VERSION OF OwnTV. It has been modified
since 2026-11-09 by Dmitry Alexandrov. Relevant dates:

  * 2026-10-21 — upstream v5.2.1, the last tagged release before the fork.
  * 2026-11-09 — snapshot of upstream main imported as this repository's
    root commit 214719f ("MyOwnTV: initial import (based on OwnTV, upstream
    history squashed)"). Upstream history is NOT part of this repository.
  * 2026-11-09 — present — all subsequent changes are this fork's own.

Principal changes (all after the import; commit ids refer to this repository):

  * The app became a live-TV-only client of RuTube's public catalogue and
    programme guide. The Xtream/M3U/Stalker source model, the mpv/libmpv
    playback engine, VOD (movies/series), trailers, downloads, catch-up,
    profiles and the file-backup UI were removed (culminating in ec31209).
    Only ExoPlayer / Media3 remains as a playback engine.
  * The TMDB and OpenSubtitles integrations, their reference Workers under
    extras/worker/, their logos and API keys were removed (cf8b0b5). The EPG
    channel matcher, the guide-candidate dialog and the player's channel
    "Sources" comparison were removed (4a962f9). The unused
    android-youtube-player dependency went with the trailer code (ec31209).
  * The database schema was rebuilt repeatedly (v4 through v8) and the
    packaged locale set was reduced to English and Russian (baa3d2b), then
    extended to four languages with Ukrainian and Belarusian (a1d246c).
  * The app was rebranded to МОЁ ТВ with a new applicationId
    (com.github.dimzon.owntv), launcher assets and moetv:// deep links;
    the current brand kit in extras/brand/ and its generators in
    extras/branding/ are this fork's own work (the original artwork is
    retained in extras/brand/legacy/).

This fork is NOT affiliated with, endorsed by, sponsored by or connected to
the original OwnTV project, ahXN00, or its contributors. "OwnTV" is used
solely to identify the work from which this one is derived.


